{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And your heart grow haughty and you forget HaShem your Elohim.</b> Pride is a cause of forgetting the principal thing, for through abundance and increase of tranquility a person's heart grows haughty and the evil inclination is roused against him, and it makes all his desires the principal thing while the desires of Heaven become secondary. It is concerning this that Solomon, peace be upon him, mentioned (Ecclesiastes 10:4): ״אם רוח המושל תעלה עליך מקומך אל תנח״. He called the force of the sphere of Mars 'ruler,' for it is the soul of the sphere, because it is the head of the governance of all the troubles and passing occurrences in the world; and the evil inclination drawn from it he called רוח — spirit — for it is a spirit of impurity. And Scripture says: if this inclination misleads you and seeks to overpower you, do not consent to it and do not listen to it, to set aside its desires rather than those of the Holy One, blessed be He, who is מקומו של עולם — the Place of the world; this is the meaning of מקומך אל תנח — 'your place do not leave.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:46:59.477543268Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}